# DTF tier manifest: pypi-conformance
# =============================================================================
# The DTF runner for the PyPI conformance corpus (conformance/corpus/pypi/*.json).
# For each scenario it stands the scenario's `mock_variant` up on the
# `mock-pypi-conf` upstream, points an AK remote pypi repo at
# http://mock-pypi-conf/<variant>, executes the scenario `steps` against AK, and
# asserts each `expect`. Adding coverage = a corpus JSON (+ maybe a mock route);
# no oracle edits. See conformance/README.md and docs/test-framework-2026.md.
#
# The mock-server pattern is credited to astral-sh/uv's pypi_proxy
# (Apache-2.0 OR MIT); see conformance/CREDITS.md.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives admin login + a repo create and
# several proxy GETs per scenario, back-to-back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mockpypi-conf"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
